    "body": "@andytom Would you like any help with this issue? Since I'm Rust rookie, not making any promises but I'd be interested in looking into it. Are you OK with suggested solutions here?\r\n\r\nSince these alternatives are good solutions, but still some lack of usabilities. All of these (included this issue) are just targets of flag `disabled`. What about other _custom_ flag _toggle-abilities_.\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n$ starship toggle <module>\r\n$ starship config toggle <module>\r\n$ starship toggle config <module>\r\n```\r\n\r\n-or-\r\n\r\nShould we concern for any other flags instead of just `disabled`? \r\n\r\n```bash\r\n$ starship config toggle git_branch.only_detached\r\n$ starship config toggle nodejs.display_private\r\n```",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
