    "body": "@Dentrax, sorry for the delay in replying, just don't seem to have enough time at the moment. Please feel free to have a go don't worry about being a new to Rust we all have to start somewhere 😄.\r\n\r\nI would be a bit hesitant to add another use to the `config` sub-command as we already use it it for updating the config file via the cli and opening the config file in an editor. So maybe add a new sub-command `toggle` with a usage something like\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ starship toggle MODULE_NAME [OPTION]\r\n```\r\n\r\n`MODULE_NAME` would just be the name of the module e.g `nodejs` or `kubernetes`\r\n\r\n`OPTION` would be an optional argument that toggling different like `only_detached`, if not set it should default to `disabled`.\r\n\r\nWhat do you think?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
