    "body": "@andytom That's sounds good! Will our brand new `toggle` command look like this eventually?\r\n\r\nThe `toggle` command feature will only work for `boolean` values. Throws error otherwise?\r\n\r\n```rust\r\n       .subcommand(\r\n            SubCommand::with_name(\"toggle\")\r\n                .about(\"Toggle a given starship module\")\r\n                .arg(\r\n                    Arg::with_name(\"name\")\r\n                        .help(\"The name of the module to be toggled\")\r\n                        .required(true),\r\n                )\r\n                .arg(\r\n                    Arg::with_name(\"value\")\r\n                        .help(\"The value of the config to be toggled\")\r\n                        .required(false),\r\n                        .required_unless(\"name\")\r\n                 ),\r\n        )\r\n```\r\n\r\ni.e.:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n$ starship toggle kubernetes # default: 'disabled'\r\n$ starship toggle git_commit only_detached # override default config key to: 'only_detached'\r\n```",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
